WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.012 --> 00:00:17.242
"Hey, Ally!"

2
00:00:17.742 --> 00:00:20.444
Later that day Jerry entered the diner with Sally.

3
00:00:20.464 --> 00:00:23.906
"We've been hearing about the cool tricks you do while waitressing.

4
00:00:24.787 --> 00:00:26.067
Can we film you doing one?"

5
00:00:26.087 --> 00:00:28.649
"Sure," Ally said.

6
00:00:28.669 --> 00:00:32.732
"It'll take my mind off the mind-reading problem," she thought.

7
00:00:34.704 --> 00:00:38.867
Ally put a few doughnuts on a plate and walked across the diner as Sally filmed her.

8
00:00:39.647 --> 00:00:42.409
Halfway across the floor, Ally made herself trip.

9
00:00:43.429 --> 00:00:45.010
She felt the plate leave her hand.

10
00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.151
She saw it fly into the air.

11
00:00:47.932 --> 00:00:51.214
But when Ally tried to activate her powers, nothing happened.

12
00:00:53.075 --> 00:00:55.616
Crash! The plate smashed onto the floor.

13
00:00:55.636 --> 00:00:58.478
"Ugh! Sorry!"

14
00:00:59.198 --> 00:01:01.740
Ally blushed in embarrassment and ran for a broom.

15
00:01:06.152 --> 00:01:07.052
"That's never happened before."

16
00:01:07.072 --> 00:01:08.073
"Don't worry about it," Jerry said.

17
00:01:08.093 --> 00:01:09.433
"Do you want to try again?"

18
00:01:09.453 --> 00:01:13.395
"Um, maybe not," Ally said.

19
00:01:13.415 --> 00:01:15.916
"I'm not having a very good day."

20
00:01:15.936 --> 00:01:18.758
"No problem," Jerry said.

21
00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:21.059
"We can try again another time."

22
00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:27.301
Jerry might not have been upset as he and Sally left, but Ally was.

23
00:01:29.742 --> 00:01:32.904
As the last customer left, she cleaned up the mess she'd made.

24
00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.163
"I don't understand what's happening to me," Ally murmured.

25
00:01:37.183 --> 00:01:41.647
"First I can't read minds, and now I can't levitate dishes."

26
00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.088
"What's that?"

27
00:01:43.408 --> 00:01:45.390
Julius asked as he entered the diner.

28
00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:48.112
"You can't meditate?

29
00:01:48.592 --> 00:01:49.193
I can teach you."

30
00:01:49.213 --> 00:01:55.137
"Oh!" Ally was embarrassed that he'd heard her, but at least he'd misunderstood.

31
00:01:55.157 --> 00:01:57.860
"Sure, thanks."

32
00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.562
"So, are you ready for our date?"

33
00:02:00.862 --> 00:02:01.683
Julius asked.

34
00:02:01.703 --> 00:02:04.057
"Date?" Ally repeated.

35
00:02:04.077 --> 00:02:08.981
"Oh gosh, you don't want go to the museum, do you?"

36
00:02:09.722 --> 00:02:10.843
Julius looked sad.

37
00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:13.965
"No, I do!"

38
00:02:14.426 --> 00:02:14.926
Ally said.

39
00:02:14.946 --> 00:02:16.948
"I'm sorry.

40
00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:21.632
I've been so distracted all day, trying to figure out who the spy is.

41
00:02:22.693 --> 00:02:23.814
But I have an idea!"

42
00:02:24.615 --> 00:02:26.556
She put the broom and dustpan away.

43
00:02:26.576 --> 00:02:33.881
"What if instead of going to the museum, we go looking for clues to track down the spy?"

44
00:02:34.841 --> 00:02:35.741
Julius grinned.

45
00:02:36.402 --> 00:02:37.282
"I love that idea!

46
00:02:37.882 --> 00:02:39.462
I've always wanted to gather intel.

47
00:02:40.603 --> 00:02:42.483
That's spy talk for getting information.

48
00:02:43.183 --> 00:02:43.984
Where should we start?"

49
00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:47.585
Ally was about to answer when Flo came out of the kitchen.

50
00:02:47.605 --> 00:02:52.446
"Ally, do you mind closing again for me?"

51
00:02:52.826 --> 00:02:53.486
Flo asked.

52
00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:57.347
"Uh, sure, but is everything okay?

53
00:02:57.847 --> 00:02:59.188
You're not sick, are you?"

54
00:02:59.568 --> 00:03:00.128
Ally asked.

55
00:03:01.116 --> 00:03:02.817
"I'm fine," Flo said.

56
00:03:04.678 --> 00:03:07.020
But she looked distracted as she left the diner.

57
00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:09.061
Ally sighed deeply.

58
00:03:09.081 --> 00:03:12.763
"I hate to admit it, Julius.

59
00:03:13.343 --> 00:03:15.425
But you could be right about Flo.

60
00:03:16.305 --> 00:03:17.806
I think we should follow her."

61
00:03:18.827 --> 00:03:19.347
He grinned.

62
00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:21.068
"I'm ready when you are!"

63
00:03:23.209 --> 00:03:27.732
Ally quickly locked up the diner, and then she and Julius ran out to follow Flo.

64
00:03:31.296 --> 00:03:34.038
They stayed behind her as she walked briskly through town.

65
00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.502
Suddenly, at a busy corner, Flo halted.

66
00:03:39.423 --> 00:03:42.425
As she waited for the traffic light to change, she looked around.

67
00:03:42.445 --> 00:03:44.647
"Quick, duck behind this mailbox!"

68
00:03:44.967 --> 00:03:45.728
Julius said.

69
00:03:47.509 --> 00:03:52.574
They waited until Flo started walking again before continuing to follow her across town.

70
00:03:55.056 --> 00:03:59.139
They followed her all the way to— Ally gasped.

71
00:04:00.844 --> 00:04:02.365
"Pepe's! She's going into Pepe's!

72
00:04:03.405 --> 00:04:05.206
Why in the world is she going in there?"

73
00:04:06.106 --> 00:04:07.447
She quickly closed her eyes.

74
00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:09.808
"I have to read Flo's mind!"

75
00:04:10.168 --> 00:04:10.628
she thought.

76
00:04:11.349 --> 00:04:14.430
But once again, all she heard was the strange static.

77
00:04:17.951 --> 00:04:20.973
Ally sighed, not wanting to believe Flo was the spy.

78
00:04:21.753 --> 00:04:23.394
But the proof was right there.

79
00:04:23.414 --> 00:04:28.256
"I can't believe this," she said to Julius.

80
00:04:29.276 --> 00:04:32.378
"Ray will be heartbroken, and so will Mateo.

81
00:04:33.299 --> 00:04:34.700
But we can't tell Barry yet.

82
00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:38.662
He's so impulsive—he could do something crazy."

83
00:04:41.544 --> 00:04:43.786
Ally and Julius hurried to Rolling Ray's.

84
00:04:47.869 --> 00:04:50.891
I thought you were going to the museum today," Mateo said.

85
00:04:50.911 --> 00:04:54.213
"Well, I'm glad you're here," Barry said.

86
00:04:54.233 --> 00:04:56.975
"You have got to taste my new dish."

87
00:04:58.095 --> 00:04:58.816
"Not right now."

88
00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:00.221
Ally waved him off.

89
00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:03.242
"I want to talk to Mateo about something."

90
00:05:03.262 --> 00:05:07.404
"After you taste my chocolate-and-peanut-butter-stuffed waffle."

91
00:05:07.705 --> 00:05:08.245
Barry said.

92
00:05:08.265 --> 00:05:10.926
"I'll taste it," Julius said.

93
00:05:10.946 --> 00:05:13.088
"Here you go."

94
00:05:13.608 --> 00:05:15.809
Barry handed Julius a waffle on a plate.

95
00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:18.991
Julius took a big bite.

96
00:05:19.011 --> 00:05:21.512
"This is delicious!

97
00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:25.354
But super messy!"

98
00:05:25.714 --> 00:05:28.636
he said as he wiped at the chocolate dripping all over his shirt.

99
00:05:29.824 --> 00:05:33.385
"So that's what you meant when you said you were going to keep this recipe close to your

100
00:05:33.445 --> 00:05:34.145
chest, Barry!"

101
00:05:34.485 --> 00:05:35.025
Ally said.

102
00:05:35.045 --> 00:05:37.826
"Ha-ha!" Barry laughed loudly.

103
00:05:37.846 --> 00:05:39.587
"That's funny, Ally!"

104
00:05:40.487 --> 00:05:42.067
Suddenly his smile fell.

105
00:05:42.087 --> 00:05:46.749
"I just realized—we can't sell something that's super messy."

106
00:05:47.429 --> 00:05:47.929
He sighed.

107
00:05:49.489 --> 00:05:51.490
"It's back to the drawing board for me!"

108
00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:58.532
"I'm so sorry, Barry," Ally said, and then she whispered to Mateo, "I need to speak with you

109
00:05:58.612 --> 00:06:00.054
alone. Now!"
